prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a farm with procedural geometry: cows/chickens/pigs roam inside a fence, with a day-night cycle, click selection, and a feeding animation. External GLB files are prohibited.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import through ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Animal Models (Procedural)]
(1) Cow: compound Box body + Sphere head + Cylinder legs + small Cone horns;
(2) Chicken: small sphere body + Cone beak + flat planar wings;
(3) Pig: round/spherical body + flat Box snout + Torus segment curly tail;
(4) 3 of each species, for 9 animals in total; each animals[].name must be unique;

[Fence]
(5) The enclosure is approximately 15×15 (XZ); animal centers must remain within the boundaries (use inner padding to prevent geometry from clipping through the fence);

[AI]
(6) Random wandering, with a random direction change every 2–5 seconds and small steps at a constant speed;

[Interaction]
(7) Select animals by raycast clicking; id="animalInfo" displays the name and type (cow/chicken/pig);
(8) id="feedBtn": play a feeding animation for the selected animal (vertical bobbing, with a sine-driven y offset over several cycles);

[Day-Night Cycle]
(9) One cycle every 30 seconds: the DirectionalLight rotates around the scene; Ambient intensity/color changes with dayTime∈[0,1);

[State Exposure (Required)]
(10) Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - animalCount (always 9)
  - animals:[{type,name,x,y,z,selected}]
  - dayTime: number (cycles through 0..1)
  - selectedAnimal: string|null

[Evaluation Helpers (Recommended)]
(11) window.__STATEPROBE_selectAnimal__(indexOrName), window.__STATEPROBE_triggerFeed__().

Output a single HTML file that can run when opened directly in a browser.
